                        "entry_id": "3ab0270c-3523-386d-85f5-fb42cc604315",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tree in the genus Aspidosperma."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c9ce89f-7443-4b80-9b09-914744a41f47",
                                "sense_id": "39d5ebe1-6b32-3402-89f4-4733a214ffd0",
                                "text": "Aspidospermas have good bending qualities."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "380054d5-9d37-3ad4-9993-21638c711a99",
                        "entry_id": "3ab0270c-3523-386d-85f5-fb42cc604315",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A group of indole alkaloids that are found in these trees, noted for a tetracyclic framework and modifications in the carbon skeleton that arise during their biosynthesis via the mevalonate pathway."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef0aa6fc-1fe6-4d43-b3a2-3f3aeb5f5484",
                                "sense_id": "380054d5-9d37-3ad4-9993-21638c711a99",
                                "text": "CA - 08869-04 Heterolytic fragmentation as applied to the synthesis of aspidosperma alkaloids"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "158400ed-1fa2-4a89-ad05-76932c223793",
                                "sense_id": "380054d5-9d37-3ad4-9993-21638c711a99",
                                "text": "The Aspidosperma alkaloids are the largest group of indole alkaloids."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "39159c62-d99f-457c-9ffc-e4b6f97933fe",
                                "sense_id": "380054d5-9d37-3ad4-9993-21638c711a99",
                                "text": "The structurally more complex aspidosperma, strychnos, and iboga alkaloids may each be derived from the corynanthe alkaloids."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "efd1aece-1558-4220-a8ee-a4e3f9d354fd",
                                "sense_id": "380054d5-9d37-3ad4-9993-21638c711a99",
                                "text": "Fortunately, however, this profusion of skeleta can be grouped into so-called borynanthe, aspidosperma, and iboga types (Geissman & Crout 1969), according to the disposition of C-atoms in the mevalonate moiety, which may have preserved the original arrangement (corynanthe) or suffered two kinds of rearrangement (aspidosperma, iboga)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
